      "mergeID": "68187de21e0f940d9f511776",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Awake() is very useful to make sure things are set up before Start(). Sometimes you want to setup stuff that are dependant on other stuff.\n\nFor example, if someone wants to save a variable of the player default run speed in their own script, this has to be executed after VRCWorldSettings (the udon graph that is attached by default to the VRCWorld object). Since VRCWorldSettings runs at start, there is no way to set up this initial variable reliably at Start because if it is executed before, it returns 0 instead of the default 4.\n\nUnless there is a reason Awake() is not exposed? Is it because maybe PlayerApi or networking local player are not ready at Awake()?",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Expose Awake() in Udon Graph",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "63fe55663fab506052b10c14",
